statement:
Let $G$ be a connected simple graph on a finite, nonempty vertex set of size $
u$, and let $k$ be a natural number. Writing $\pi_k(G)$ for the number of distinct proper $k$-colourings of $G$, one has
\[ \pi_k(G) \le k(k-1)^{
u-1}, \]
and moreover, if $k \ge 3$, then equality $\pi_k(G) = k(k-1)^{
u-1}$ holds if and only if $G$ is a tree.
